          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I keep thinking about killing myself and I don't know who to talk to.",
          "answer": "**Seek emergency care now.** What you have described can be a medical emergency. Call emergency services or go to an emergency department immediately. Do not wait to see whether it improves, and do not drive yourself.\n\n**This is an emergency. Please reach out for help now.** If you are in immediate danger, or you have already acted on these thoughts, call your local emergency number right away.\n\n- **In the United States:** call or text **988** to reach the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline. It is free and available 24 hours a day.\n- **Elsewhere:** most countries have an equivalent crisis line. Look up the number for your area now, so you have it ready.\n- **A trusted person:** tell someone you're with, or a friend or family member, that you're having these thoughts. You don't have to explain it perfectly. You can say, \"I'm not okay and I need you to be with me.\"\n\nIf you can, stay with someone or move somewhere you're not alone until you've reached a person. If you have anything nearby that you might use to hurt yourself, put distance between you and it, or ask someone to hold it for you.\n\nThoughts of suicide need to reach a person immediately, not wait for a routine appointment. This comes from the guidance on thoughts of suicide or self-harm (red-flag-suicidal-ideation). I can't tell how much danger you are in from a text, so please use one of these routes now.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
